	.SBTTL	SLOPT - SL's options for the MS 0515's monitors

; DEC's SL keeps a table of impure areas, one a job, eight by default.  The
; monitors of the MS 0515 are single-job ones: one entry, and sixteen bytes
; of the resident handler back.

Job$	= 1

; DEC's picture of a VT52's keypad, which PF2 draws, is half a block of the
; resident handler.  Without it PF2 is a line pointing at the manual - and
; here the keys' own text, kept in the overlay (SLKEY.MAC, SLOVL.MAC).

HelpB$	= 0
